{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **November 6, 2026**:\n\n- **Fixed transaction fees** generally cover creation/redemption processing: custody, transfer-agent, clearing, settlement and related administrative costs. Usually charged per order, not per creation unit.\n- **Variable fees** generally offset trading-related costs—commissions, bid–ask spreads, market impact, taxes and foreign-exchange costs—particularly for cash transactions or cash substitutions, protecting existing shareholders against dilution.\n- **Who bears them:** The submitting authorized participant (AP) generally owes these charges and may pass them to its client. Unrecovered costs remain with the fund and its shareholders.\n- **Recipients may differ:** For example, the fixed fee may go to the custodian or another service provider, while the variable fee goes to the fund. The prospectus/SAI controls.\n\n**Worth knowing:** These charges are not themselves AP compensation. An AP’s separately negotiated client commissions/service fees, trading spreads and arbitrage profits are distinct."}}
